From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:55:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: List the TCC activation offset under
 Thermal

Energy Saver > Thermal gets the TCC activation offset of the CPU code,
next to the cooling policy: the processor throttles that many degrees C
below TjMax. Default 0, as up to now. Listed only on the processors
with a programmable offset; the W541 and the T440p share the menu.

TEST=Host syntax check of cfr.c with the configuration of the ThinkPad
W541.
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
index c4e4bb2076..7b96c01b73 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
@@ -419,6 +419,7 @@ static const struct sm_object energy_thermal = SM_DECLARE_FORM({
 	.ui_name	= "Thermal",
 	.obj_list	= (const struct sm_object *[]) {
 		&cooling_policy,
+		&tcc_offset,
 		NULL
 	},
 });
-- 
